(  ===================================================================  )
(  TUTORIAL PART - your first program on the EMCO PC Turn 50            )
(  ===================================================================  )
(                                                                       )
(  Makes a simple stepped pin from 12 mm aluminium bar:                 )
(                                                                       )
(        |<--- 10 ---->|<--- 12 --->|                                   )
(        +-------------+                                                )
(        |   O8        |    O12     |         <- chuck/collet this end  )
(        +-------------+------------+                                   )
(                                                                       )
(  Stock      : 12 mm aluminium round, ESX 25 collet                    )
(  Sticking out: at least 30 mm from the collet face                    )
(  Tools      : T1 right-hand turning, T3 parting blade                 )
(  Run time   : about three minutes                                     )
(                                                                       )
(  READ THIS BEFORE RUNNING IT ANYWHERE NEAR METAL                      )
(  ---------------------------------------------------------------     )
(  Work zero G54 is set at the FACE of the stock, on the centreline.     )
(  You set that by touching off - see docs/40-operator-guide.md.        )
(  If you have not touched off, this program will cut air or crash.     )
(                                                                       )
(  Run it in the simulator first. Every time. It costs nothing.         )
(  ===================================================================  )

G21          ( millimetres                                              )
G18          ( XZ plane - the only sensible plane on a lathe            )
G40          ( cutter compensation off                                  )
G90          ( absolute coordinates                                     )
G95          ( feed per revolution - mm/rev, the natural unit for turning)
G7           ( DIAMETER mode: an X value means diameter, not radius.     )
             ( This is how the original EMCO control worked and how the  )
             ( drawings are dimensioned, so it is what we use.           )

(  --- safety line: retract before anything else happens ---            )
G53 G0 X48   ( machine coordinates: fully retracted, clear of the work  )

(  =================================================================    )
(  1. FACE THE END                                                      )
(  =================================================================    )
T1 M6        ( right-hand turning tool                                  )
G54          ( work offset: Z0 at the face, X0 on the centreline        )
S1200 M3     ( 1200 rpm clockwise - belt step 2, 200-2000 rpm on the real  )
             ( machine, which you change BY HAND before starting        )
G0 X14 Z1    ( approach: 1 mm clear of the face, just outside the stock )
G1 X-0.4 F0.08  ( face across centre. Going slightly past zero leaves    )
                ( no little pip in the middle.                          )
G0 Z1        ( back off in Z before retracting, so we do not rub        )
G0 X14

(  =================================================================    )
(  2. TURN THE 8 mm DIAMETER, 10 mm LONG                                )
(  =================================================================    )
(  Two roughing passes then a finish pass. Aluminium is soft but the    )
(  machine is small - 1 mm depth of cut per pass on diameter is plenty. )

G0 X10.4 Z0.5     ( first rough pass, leaving 0.4 mm on diameter        )
G1 Z-10 F0.10
G0 X11            ( retract clear before returning                      )
G0 Z0.5

G0 X8.4           ( second rough pass                                   )
G1 Z-10 F0.10
G0 X9
G0 Z0.5

G0 X8             ( finish pass: full depth, slower feed, better finish )
G1 Z-10 F0.05
G1 X12            ( face the shoulder outward                          )
G0 X14

(  =================================================================    )
(  3. CHAMFER THE FREE END                                              )
(  =================================================================    )
G0 X6 Z1
G1 X8 Z-0.5 F0.05  ( a 45 degree chamfer, 1 mm across                   )
G0 X14

(  =================================================================    )
(  4. PART OFF AT 22 mm                                                 )
(  =================================================================    )
(  Parting is the most likely operation to go wrong on a small lathe.   )
(  Slow the spindle down, feed steadily, and do not let it dwell.       )

M5                 ( stop before changing tools                         )
T3 M6              ( parting blade, 2 mm wide                           )
S800 M3            ( slower for parting                                 )
G0 X14 Z-22        ( 22 mm from the face: 10 mm step + 12 mm body       )
G1 X0.5 F0.04      ( part down to nearly centre - the last bit snaps    )
G0 X14             ( retract immediately                                )

(  =================================================================    )
(  5. FINISH UP                                                         )
(  =================================================================    )
M5                 ( spindle off                                        )
G53 G0 X48 Z0      ( return to the reference corner, clear of everything)
M30                ( program end and rewind                             )
